---
config:
  theme: default
title: Job Search and Discovery Sequence
---
sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant JobsPage
    participant API
    participant Backend
    participant NLPMatcher
    participant MongoDB
    
    %% Initial Page Load
    Note over User,MongoDB: Initial Page Load
    User->>JobsPage: Navigate to /jobs
    JobsPage->>API: GET /api/jobs
    API->>Backend: Request with JWT token
    Backend->>MongoDB: db.jobs.find().sort(postedDate: -1)
    MongoDB-->>Backend: Return all jobs (paginated)
    Backend-->>API: 200 OK + jobs array
    API-->>JobsPage: Jobs data
    JobsPage->>User: Display job cards
    
    %% Apply Filters
    Note over User,MongoDB: Apply Filters
    User->>JobsPage: Select filters:<br/>Role, Location, Salary, Remote
    JobsPage->>JobsPage: Update local state
    JobsPage->>API: GET /api/jobs?role=Developer&location=Remote
    API->>Backend: Request with query params
    Backend->>MongoDB: db.jobs.find(query).sort()
    MongoDB-->>Backend: Filtered jobs
    Backend-->>API: 200 OK + filtered jobs
    API-->>JobsPage: Update job list
    JobsPage->>User: Display filtered results
    
    %% Search with NLP
    Note over User,MongoDB: Search with NLP Matching
    User->>JobsPage: Enter search: "React developer"
    JobsPage->>API: POST /api/jobs/search<br/>{query: "React developer"}
    API->>Backend: Search request
    Backend->>NLPMatcher: Match query against user profile
    NLPMatcher->>NLPMatcher: Tokenize query
    NLPMatcher->>NLPMatcher: Extract keywords
    NLPMatcher->>MongoDB: Get user skills & preferences
    MongoDB-->>NLPMatcher: User profile data
    NLPMatcher->>MongoDB: Find jobs matching keywords
    MongoDB-->>NLPMatcher: Candidate jobs
    NLPMatcher->>NLPMatcher: Calculate match scores
    NLPMatcher-->>Backend: Ranked jobs with scores
    Backend-->>API: 200 OK + matched jobs
    API-->>JobsPage: Display results with match %
    JobsPage->>User: Show ranked jobs
    
    %% View Job Details
    Note over User,MongoDB: View Job Details
    User->>JobsPage: Click job card
    JobsPage->>API: GET /api/jobs/:id
    API->>Backend: Fetch single job
    Backend->>MongoDB: db.jobs.findById(id)
    MongoDB-->>Backend: Job document
    Backend-->>API: 200 OK + job details
    API-->>JobsPage: Full job data
    JobsPage->>User: Display job modal/page
    
    %% Save Job
    Note over User,MongoDB: Save Job for Later
    User->>JobsPage: Click "Save" button
    JobsPage->>API: POST /api/jobs/:id/save
    API->>Backend: Save job request
    Backend->>MongoDB: db.users.updateOne()<br/>$addToSet savedJobs
    MongoDB-->>Backend: User updated
    Backend-->>API: 200 OK
    API-->>JobsPage: Update UI state
    JobsPage->>User: Show "Saved" confirmation

